import React, { useState, useMemo, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from 'react';

/*
  =============================================================================
  === EXCEL-STYLE HIGH-PERFORMANCE GRID (V9) ===
  0. Id matching: the log's craa5_equipmentguid is the equipment's craa5_aa_assetsid, and the calendar
     shows every log entry stored against an equipment id. Old entries whose id is blank or matches no
     equipment are matched by equipment name (amber markers). Logs load per visible equipment and month, never the whole table.
     Payload Diagnostics has a log check and an equipment lookup that show what Dataverse returns.
  1. Area Pagination (New): When expanded, Areas now limit equipment to 10 items.
     Individual "Next" buttons added per Area to navigate large equipment sets.
  2. Room Pagination: Main view continues to handle top-level Room pagination (5 per page).
  3. Focused Popup Dialog: Scoped views remain available for isolated analysis.
  4. Master Sticky Headers: Headers remain pinned at the top of the grid viewport.
  5. Frozen Hierarchy: Left-side directory remains pinned during horizontal scroll.
  6. Frequency medallion, inside the equipment cell: the cleaning frequencies set on the equipment (D MW W M Q S A),
     a letter turning red when the last clean of that kind is outside the frequency, from the log rows loaded so far.
  7. Room and area rows, by the done-or-blank method: a check on every day on which any of their equipment was
     cleaned, and a small progress bar beside the name (green check: everything read was cleaned in the months on
     screen, yellow: some cleaned and some missed, red: nothing cleaned, grey: not read yet) with a Read button.
  8. Paperwork: a log row with a picture or file attached shows a paper clip on its marker; a click opens the
     picture in a popout with a Download button. The bytes come from the Dataverse File column, not the row.
  9. Company theme (blue / yellow / red), shared with the other apps in this project.
 10. Completion percentages: in full mode (see 13) four rows of the MSS under the day headers carry them (done % and number
     not done, for the day and, on every Sunday, for that Monday-to-Sunday week). The rest is on the Completion tab (see 14). Every
     frequency letter on an equipment is one job per period (see COMPLETION PERCENTAGES below).
 11. Line Downtime tab, after Payload Diagnostics: the production lines (area plus line number) as the production plan
     (craa5__aa_prd_schd) names them, with the MSS areas whose equipment follow each line, the date ranges a line is down
     besides (Off schedule, one day is fine) and a preview of the next five weeks. A line that is not in the plan can be
     added by hand, with scheduled weekdays. What is typed is saved in this browser (see LINE DOWNTIME).
 12. Line rules (see LINE RULES): equipment in an area a line follows has a Daily job only on a day that line had downtime,
     one Daily job for a stretch of days in a row the line did not produce (a down weekend included), and mid-week and weekly jobs
     only in a week it ran, all from the plan. A stretch of idle days over New Year is judged whole (the calendars are built
     ten weeks beyond the year on each side, and the plan is read for those weeks too), in the year its last day falls in.
 13. Two views, both titled MSS. The plain MSS (the default) shows only the schedule: rooms, areas, equipment, the frequency
     medallion, the done-or-blank days and the room and area bars. Clicking the CJ Schwan's logo turns it to inverse colours and
     enters full mode (click again to leave it), which adds the daily and weekly completion rows under the day headers (percent
     done and number not done for each day and for each Sunday's Monday-to-Sunday week). Nothing for those figures is computed or
     read (the production plan included) while the plain MSS is showing. In full mode the figures wait, dimmed, for the production
     plan to be read before they count as final.
 14. Completion tab (after Line Downtime): the figure for the slicer months and for the year to date (with Read year to date), what
     counts (untick a room or an area, or leave out one equipment, to take it out of every percentage; kept in this browser, see
     COMPLETION SELECTION), and Top missed: equipment, areas or rooms ranked by jobs not done over the slicer months or the year
     so far, narrowed by frequency letter or to one room or area, where the frequency letters of an equipment can be switched and
     saved to craa5_aa_assets after a confirmation. Computed only while the tab is open.
 16. Ecosystem data contract 1.0 (ecosystem/data-contract.md, the HUB SHARED block below): a log row's day is its shift date
     (craa5_shiftdate, else the first 10 characters of craa5_lastcleaned, never moved by the time zone); its kind of clean is
     craa5_cleankind when the row has one (daily, midweek, eow, monthly, ...; a daily clean no longer counts as the mid-week or
     monthly job), else the old craa5_daily / weekly / monthly flags as before; rows with one craa5_completionkey count once;
     deactivated rows (an undone Done) are left out. Language and theme use the shared hub_lang / hub_theme switches.
 15. More of the screen for the grid (see VIEW): slimmer header, slicer and margins; COMPACT (on by default: shorter rows and header
     tiers); FOCUS (the title row folds into one slim bar with the month chips and the buttons, on every tab); TODAY (scrolls the grid
     to today's column, once on its own when the grid opens); LATE ONLY (hides the rows known to be done on time in the pages that
     are open); a tint on the day column under the pointer; the Prev/Next of an area stays in view while the grid is scrolled sideways.
  =============================================================================
*/

