                <p style={{ color: '#64748b' }}>Completion percentages: every frequency letter on an equipment is one job per period (D per day, MW and W per Monday-to-Sunday week, M per month, Q per quarter, S per half year, A per year). A job is done when a clean of at least that kind (same ranks as the medallion) is dated inside its period, missed when every month it touches has been read for the equipment and there is none, and left out while a month is unread. The MSS in full mode (click the CJ Schwan's logo; the plain MSS shows none of this and reads no production plan) has two rows under the day headers per kind: the day rows show the Daily jobs of that day (done % and number not done); the Sunday rows every daily, mid-week and weekly job of that week. The Completion tab has the rest: the figure for the slicer months and for the year so far (which also count the monthly, quarterly and annual jobs), what counts (a room, an area or an equipment can be left out of every percentage, kept in this browser), and Top missed (equipment, area or room, ranked by jobs not done, with the frequency letters of an equipment editable and saved to craa5_aa_assets after you confirm). With the production plan read, equipment in an area a line follows (Line Downtime tab) has {LR_RULE_TEXT}; a week no plan row reaches is left out. All other equipment keeps a Daily job every day and a weekly job every week. The totals count the jobs whose period ended inside the months on screen, and since 1 January (a period still running counts only once done). A figure in italics is for a day or week not over yet, a dotted one leaves out jobs of equipment not read yet. 90% and above is green, 70% and above yellow, below red (PCT_GOOD and PCT_WARN at the top of the file); DAILY_ON lists the weekdays on which a Daily job falls due. The rows on the MSS follow the search filter; the Completion tab does not. Only equipment with a cleaning frequency has jobs (the room and area bars, Load all and Equipment loaded count every equipment). They cover only the months read from the log so far: a month not read yet is left out, not counted as missed, and a job that reaches into a month not read yet (a quarterly or annual job, the first week of the year or of the months on screen) counts only once it is done. Read year to date also reads the December before the year, where the first week of the year starts.</p>
